    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1036">

                <pb facs="0893" n="777" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg777"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.113/364.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-04-09T22:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 9, 1912—10 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The shipment of arms for the American colony will leave Vera Cruz to-night. Owing
                    to the duties—about $7,500 gold, and the Chargé for the special train and
                    escort, about $750 gold—the price of each rifle, with 100 rounds of ammunition,
                    will amount to about $20 gold.</p>
                <p>No guns or ammunition will be delivered by the military attaché except upon
                    payment either by the committee or by individuals.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
